Understood, Hugo. That realistically moves go-live to 29 March.

So, for everyone on this thread: as of today the course assistant pilot is
building in dummy-data mode. Synthetic course shells and fake student
accounts only. No real student data goes into the tenant, the context API or
any test course until your security review is approved. Anything that needs
real data is blocked on that review.

What doesn't change: Dmitri keeps building the context API against spec v1
with the synthetic shells; it's still due 5 March. Tenant and SSO setup carry
on in parallel. None of that needs real records.

Bart - for awareness. 22 March is the date most people on campus have
heard, so expect the odd question.

If anyone wants to argue about what counts as "real data", let's take that
offline.

Yusra

